Agent-driven UI is bidirectional. The agent pushes state to the component; the
component sends user actions back. Both halves are always generated together.

**Python tool** — emits the UI interaction and waits for the response:
```python
from __future__ import annotations
from typing import Annotated, Any, Optional

from mozaiksai.core.workflow.ui_tools import UIToolError, use_ui_tool

async def save_<name>(
    context_variables: Annotated[Optional[Any], "AG2 context"] = None,
    chat_id: Annotated[Optional[str], "Current chat id"] = None,
    workflow_name: Annotated[Optional[str], "Active workflow name"] = None,
) -> dict[str, Any]:
    """Render <Component> and wait for the user's response."""
    data: Any = {}
    if context_variables is not None:
        getter = getattr(context_variables, "get", None)
        if callable(getter):
            data = getter("structured_output") or {}
        else:
            raw = getattr(context_variables, "data", None)
            if isinstance(raw, dict):
                data = raw.get("structured_output") or {}

    if not isinstance(data, dict):
        data = {}

    payload = {
        "title": data.get("title") or "<Title>",
        "summary": data.get("summary") or "",
        "items": data.get("items") or [],
    }

    try:
        return await use_ui_tool(
            "<Component>",  # must exactly match tools.yaml -> ui.component
            payload,
            chat_id=chat_id,
            workflow_name=workflow_name or "<WorkflowName>",
        )
    except UIToolError as exc:
        return {"status": "error", "message": str(exc)}


__all__ = ["save_<name>"]
```

**React component** — receives shell props, renders UI, sends actions back:
```jsx
import { useState } from 'react'
import { Alert, Button, Panel, StatusPill } from '@mozaiks/chat-ui/ui'

export default function <Component>({
  payload = {},
  onResponse,
  onCancel,
  toolName,
  toolCallId,
  workflowName,
  componentId = '<Component>',
}) {
  const [submitting, setSubmitting] = useState(false)
  const items = Array.isArray(payload.items) ? payload.items : []

  const submit = async (action) => {
    setSubmitting(true)
    try {
      await onResponse?.({
        status: 'submitted',
        action,
        data: { action, tool_name: toolName, tool_call_id: toolCallId, workflowName, componentId },
      })
    } finally {
      setSubmitting(false)
    }
  }

  return (
    <Panel
      title={payload.title || '<Title>'}
      action={<StatusPill label={payload.status || 'ready'} tone="primary" />}
    >
      <div className="space-y-4">
        <span className="text-xs text-muted-foreground">
          {workflowName || 'GeneratedWorkflow'}
        </span>
        {payload.error ? <Alert message={payload.error} variant="warning" /> : null}
        <p className="text-sm text-muted-foreground">
          {payload.summary || 'Review the generated output before continuing.'}
        </p>
        <div className="space-y-2">
          {items.map((item, index) => (
            <div
              key={index}
              className="rounded-lg border border-border bg-card/60 px-3 py-2 text-sm text-foreground"
            >
              {typeof item === 'string' ? item : item?.label || item?.title || `Item ${index + 1}`}
            </div>
          ))}
        </div>
        <div className="flex flex-wrap gap-3">
          <Button
            label="Approve"
            onClick={() => submit('approve')}
            variant="primary"
            loading={submitting}
          />
          <Button
            label="Needs Revision"
            onClick={() => submit('revise')}
            variant="secondary"
            loading={submitting}
          />
          {onCancel ? (
            <Button
              label="Cancel"
              onClick={() => onCancel({ status: 'cancelled' })}
              variant="ghost"
            />
          ) : null}
        </div>
      </div>
    </Panel>
  )
}
```

**CSS token rules** (all generated React):
- Named imports only: `import { useState } from 'react'` — never `import React from 'react'`
- Semantic tokens only: `bg-primary`, `text-foreground`, `bg-card`,
